  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 155 AM MDT Sat Sep 12 2026\n\nToday through Mon night...Canadian trough continues to move \neastward, but the pressure gradient is still strong enough to \nkeep wind gusty. With the trough departing, temperatures will \nwarm compared to Fri. This will, in turn, lower humidity. The \noverlap of critical humidity below 15 percent, wind gusts over \n25 mph, and critical fuels will be Fire Weather Zone 427, the \nsouthern hills and Raft River region. There is some instability \nand moisture in the Bear Lake basin that could trigger showers \nand thunderstorms today. \n\nA low will be moving into the panhandle late tonight, and \nslowly moving into extreme northwest MT on Sun. This puts\neastern Idaho in the position of having a jet streak overhead.\nCurrent expectations are that Wind Advisory thresholds will be\nmet in the afternoon and early evening in Zones 51 and 52, the\nLava Beds and the Arco area/Mud Lake Desert.\n\nThe low moves into north central MT Sun night, reducing the \nwind and allowing colder air to move into east Idaho. \nSurprisingly, there is quite a bit of cold dry air and very \nlittle cloudiness is expected with the surface cold front, and \neven less precipitation. \n\nHigh temperatures, after warming today, will cool 10 to 16 deg F\non Sun, and another 1 to 7 deg F from Sun to Mon.",
